1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,990
Was the Prophet (peace be upon him) ever affected by sihr?

2
00:00:03,220 --> 00:00:04,400
And how did Allah cure him?

3
00:00:05,310 --> 00:00:08,210
‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated in Sahih al-Bukhari that

4
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:11,620
a man from the Jews cast sihr on the Prophet (peace be upon him),

5
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,950
so that he would imagine he had done something he had not done.

6
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:18,230
The Prophet (peace be upon him) called upon his Lord much,

7
00:00:18,640 --> 00:00:20,340
and then Allah informed him of what had afflicted him,

8
00:00:20,650 --> 00:00:22,020
and the two Mu‘awwidhatayn were revealed.

9
00:00:22,620 --> 00:00:25,210
Each time he recited a verse, a knot came undone,

10
00:00:25,520 --> 00:00:27,700
until he stood up as if released from a bond.

11
00:00:28,430 --> 00:00:29,330
Sihr is real,

12
00:00:29,630 --> 00:00:32,440
but its remedy follows the guidance of the Prophet (peace be upon him): supplication to Allah

13
00:00:32,770 --> 00:00:33,650
and reciting the two Mu‘awwidhatayn,

14
00:00:33,950 --> 00:00:35,310
not cryptic charms or sorcery.

15
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:41,910
So do not fear sihr to the point of abandoning treatment, and do not blame everything that befalls you on it.

16
00:00:42,410 --> 00:00:45,930
Protect yourself with the adhkar, and see a doctor if the symptoms persist.

17
00:00:46,410 --> 00:00:49,560
Share this story with someone you love, and follow the channel.

